    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3ca9a85_6fef796e",
        "filename": "driver/charger/bq25710.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-08T16:35:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By default prochot is a pulse, where the pulse width can be modified via one of the registers. However, in pulse mode if the condition that triggered prochot persists, then the pulse is automatically extended until that condition is no longer present.\n\nThere is a control bit, that if set, would extend the prochot pulse always (independent of the triggering condition) and needs to be explicitly cleared by a write from the EC. But, we do not use this mode.",
      "parentUuid": "8c38c106_0910046d",
